{{- /* The Antigravity plugin's hooks.json body, rendered.

       It lives here rather than only in the plugin tree so the agy plugin
       reconciler can fingerprint the SAME rendered bytes the CLI serves. The
       tree's own hooks.json.tmpl is a one-line includeTemplate wrapper, so its
       source text never changes when this partial does; a fingerprint over the
       wrapper alone would freeze while the deployed declaration moved.

       Antigravity has no session-start event. PreInvocation fires before every
       model call and its response injects steps, so it is the delivery point;
       the binary re-injects the whole envelope each time rather than once.

       PreToolUse carries the launch gate. Its matcher is deliberately `*`.
       Antigravity derives a tool name from its step type, so a name pinned
       today can be renamed by an upgrade — and the matcher is evaluated BEFORE
       the handler, so a stale name means the gate never runs at all while every
       test here stays green. The adapter decides instead, on whether the event
       carries a command. Codex's declaration omits its matcher for the same
       reason.

       Handlers run through `sh -c`, so the absolute path is shell-quoted: a
       home directory containing a space would otherwise break the command
       before the binary could fail open.

       Timeouts are whole seconds. The injection side must exceed the binary's
       own guide-fetch budget or a lead would lose its envelope to the harness
       clock rather than to a missing guide; the gate side is smaller because it
       is paid on every tool call.

       Takes the chezmoi context as its argument. */ -}}
{{- $binary := joinPath .chezmoi.homeDir ".local/libexec/orchestration-hook" -}}
{{- $quoted := printf "'%s'" (replace "'" "'\\''" $binary) -}}
{
  "dotfiles-orchestration": {
    "PreInvocation": [
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": {{ printf "%s hook --harness agy" $quoted | quote }},
        "timeout": 15
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": {{ printf "%s guard --harness agy" $quoted | quote }},
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
